Two libraries, two searches — and it is his edition on the About page
=====================================================================

Tools & skills had one search over one undifferentiated pile. The app discovers the Hermes profiles on
this machine by convention, so that "pile" is the app's handful of bundled skills plus the agent's
whole procedural library — hundreds of entries — and one search over both made the smaller set look
like the whole thing.

Now there are two panels, each with its own search:

  * **QuixiDesk tools & skills** — what ships with the app and what is in your data directory
  * **Hermes** — the agent's library, discovered from ~/.hermes/profiles/*/skills, grouped by area
    (the `area/name` prefix), with area chips to narrow it and a live "N of M" count

A skill's chip also appears on its card, so a result tells you which library it came from without a
label saying so.

About stops describing someone else's product:

  - "An independent native AI workspace built with Rust."
  + VolkDude
  + VolkDude's QuixiDesk
  + "A Linux desktop for running an agent against your own machine: your files, your models, your
     storage."

It also stops claiming independence it does not have, and says what it needs instead: GTK and the
system webview, and that it reports what is missing rather than pretending.
